{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5ValueMapRigidity","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHabiroInfiniteRigidity"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.electron_block_pinned_all_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.electron_block_pinned_all_roots","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L177-L182","doc":"**The electron block, pinned with no degree hypothesis at all.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.muon_block_pinned_all_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.muon_block_pinned_all_roots","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L165-L175","doc":"**The muon block, pinned with no degree hypothesis at all.**\n\nAgreement across the full fibre-root family `2cos(π/(N+2))` forces equality outright.\nThis is `bwsd`'s dissolution applied to a concrete physical block —\n`eq_of_habiro_root_agreement` had no consumer anywhere in the corpus, and the `n = 5`\ntheorems went on carrying the hypothesis it removes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.four_roots_insufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.four_roots_insufficient","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L156-L161","doc":"**Four roots are not enough**, so five is the threshold rather than merely a\nsufficient count: with the measured degree bound `< 5`, `muon_block_pinned_level6`\ncloses at five and this fails at four. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.no_finite_root_set_suffices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.no_finite_root_set_suffices","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L136-L154","doc":"**No finite set of roots suffices without a degree bound.**\n\nFor any finite `S` and any value map `V`, the polynomial `V + ∏_{s ∈ S}(X − s)` differs\nfrom `V` and agrees with it on all of `S`. So a finite root family can only ever pin the\ngauge row *together with* a degree hypothesis — which is precisely why `bwsd`'s\ndissolution had to go through the infinite family rather than a bigger finite one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.electron_block_pinned_level6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.electron_block_pinned_level6","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L121-L129","doc":"**The electron block is pinned by level-6 root agreement** — same instance for\n`d((3,1,1)) = t⁴ − 3t² + 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.muon_block_pinned_level6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.muon_block_pinned_level6","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L108-L119","doc":"**The muon block is pinned by level-6 root agreement.**\n\nFive fold points `2cos(kπ/6)`, `k = 1..5`, against a degree-`< 5` gauge row. One root\nfewer than `KeystoneN5ValueMapRigidity.muon_block_pinned_level7`, and one level lower,\nwhich is a strictly weaker demand on the open WRT agreement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.n5_degrees_lt_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.n5_degrees_lt_five","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L93-L104","doc":"**The four `n = 5` block degrees are `< 5`**, not merely `< 6`.\n\nSharpens `KeystoneN5ValueMapRigidity.n5_degrees_lt_six`, whose bound was chosen to\nmatch the six level-7 fold points rather than the polynomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.mark_six_block_is_not_qi_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.mark_six_block_is_not_qi_six","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L77-L91","doc":"**The mark-6 block is not `[6]`.**\n\n`d((3,1,1)) = [5] + 1` and `[6]` take the same value `6` at `t = 2` — which is what the\nmark names — and are different polynomials. Reading the mark as an index into the\nquantum integers is what puts a degree-`5` block in the `n = 5` list, and there is\nnone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.qiSix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.qiSix","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneN5LevelSixSuffices.lean#L74-L75","doc":"`[6]` as a Chebyshev polynomial in the fold variable: `t⁵ − 4t³ + 3t`, degree `5`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}